.TH PENGUIN-CPP 1 "October 2026" "Penguin cpp @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
penguin-cpp \- simple C and C++ IDE for learning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B penguin-cpp
[\fB\-c\fR \fIdirectory\fR] [\fIfile\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Penguin cpp
is an integrated development environment for C and C++, a Linux port of
Dev-C++. It edits source files and projects, builds them with
.BR gcc (1)
and
.BR make (1),
runs programs in a terminal window and debugs them with
.BR gdb (1).
.PP
Each \fIfile\fR is opened in the editor; a \fB.dev\fR file is opened as a
project. If the IDE is already running with the same settings, the files are
opened in that window instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " directory"
Keep the settings in \fIdirectory\fR instead of the user's settings folder.
A relative \fIdirectory\fR starts from the current directory. It must be the
first option.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/penguin-cpp/
Settings, color schemes and the list of trusted projects
(\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is honored).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/penguin-cpp/Templates/
Project templates the user creates (\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME\fR is honored).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/penguin-cpp/
Temporary files (\fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME\fR is honored).
.TP
.I /usr/share/penguin-cpp/
Languages, templates and help that come with the IDE.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gcc (1),
.BR g++ (1),
.BR make (1),
.BR gdb (1),
.BR astyle (1),
.BR clang-format (1)
.PP
https://github.com/JuanFranG/Penguin-cpp
